        <cell><m>\vphantom{\Huge{M}}</m> </cell>
        <cell><m>\vphantom{\Huge{M}}</m> </cell>
    </row>
    <row halign="center">
        <cell>It costs Corporal Motors $500,000 to outfit their new car line.  The company used the equation <m>P(c)=2500c-500,000</m> to detrmine the amount of profit <m>P</m> earned from the sale of <m>c</m> cars. <m>\vphantom{\Huge{M}}</m> </cell>
        <cell><m>\vphantom{\Huge{M}}</m> </cell>
        <cell> </cell>
    </row>
