<page>
<exercise>
    <introduction>
        <p>
            Each story below will either ask for a calculation to be done or an equation to be found.  Do what is asked, and leave the other column blank.
        </p>
    </introduction>
 <tabular top="minor" bottom="medium" left="major" right="major">
        <col width="10%" halign="center"/>
        <col width="45%"/>
        <col width="45%"/>
    <row header="yes" halign="center">
        <cell>Story</cell>
        <cell>Calculation</cell>
        <cell>Equation</cell>
    </row>
    <row halign="center">
        <cell>Maui begins working at Macy's.  She will be paid a daily amount plus a commission of her total sales.  The equation <m>P(s)=0.10s+15</m> represents the amount Maui will make based on her total sales where <m>P</m> is the amount of money she makes in one day, and <m>s</m> is her total sales.  How much will Maui make if she sells $650? <m>\vphantom{\Huge{M}}</m>     </cell>
        <cell><fill cols="45" rows="6"/></cell>
        <cell>---<fill cols="45" rows="6"/></cell>
    </row>
    <row halign="center">
        <cell>Alejandra paints faces at kids' parties to earn extra money.  The equation <m>M(f)=2.5f+12</m> represents the relationship between the money <m>M</m> she makes after painting <m>f</m> faces.  Alejandra wants to buy a new pair of Uggs that cost $119.50.  How many faces does she need to paint in order to pay for her Uggs? <m>\vphantom{\Huge{M}}</m></cell>
        <cell> </cell>
        <cell>---</cell>
    </row>
    <row halign="center">
        <cell>Archie is learning to scuba dive.  The equation <m>D(L)=20L+15</m> represents the depth, <m>D</m> he can dive, in feet, based on the number of lessons, <m>L</m> he has taken.  How deep can Archie dive after he has taken 13 lessons? <m>\vphantom{\Huge{M}}</m></cell>
        <cell> </cell>
        <cell>---</cell>
    </row>
    <row halign="center">
        <cell>Stormy joins a gym.  She pays $15 for the membership and $6 for each session she does at the gym.  Write and equation that models the relationship between the cost <m>C</m> that STormy pays, and the number of sessions <m>n</m> that she does at the gym.  Write the equation in function notation. <m>\vphantom{\Huge{M}}</m></cell>
        <cell>---</cell>
        <cell> </cell>
    </row>
    <row halign="center">
        <cell>Michael is draining his pool for the winter,  There are 3200 gallons of water in the pool and it is decreasing at a rate of 200 gallons per hour.  Write an equation to represent the relationship between the amount of water <m>A</m> in the pool, and the number of hours <m>h</m> the poos has been draining.  Write the equation in function notation. <m>\vphantom{\Huge{M}}</m></cell>
        <cell>---</cell>
        <cell> </cell>
    </row>
    <row halign="center">
        <cell>Mama B is planning Thanksgiving dinner.  The number of pounds of turkey she will buy depends on the number of people she invites to dinner.  If she invites 12 people, she needs to buy a 15 pound turkey.  If she invites 20 people, she needs to buy a 25 pound turkey.  Write an equation to represent the relationship between the number of guests <m>g</m> and the pounds <m>P</m> of turkey needed.  Write the equation in function notation. </cell>
        <cell>---</cell>
        <cell> </cell>
    </row>
   </tabular>
</exercise> 
<exercise>
    <introduction>
    <p>
        Wyatt joins a streaming service.  She pays $15 to set up the service and $4.99 per month to use the service.  
    </p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace="0.01in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                If <m>C</m> is the cost of the service, and <m>m</m> is the number of months using the service, find <m>C(6)</m> and explain what it means in the context of the problem.
            </p>
        </statement>
    <answer>
        <p>
            <m>C(6)=15+4.99*6=44.94</m>  
        </p>
        <p>
            If Wyatt uses the streaming service for 6 months, her cost will be $44.94.
        </p>
    </answer>
    </task>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                What do the domain values represent?  
            </p>
        </statement>
        <answer>
            <p>
                The number of months using the service
            </p>
        </answer>
    </task>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                What is the practical domain; answer in interval or inequality notation? (does infinity makes sense?)
            </p>
        </statement>
        <answer>
            <p>
                Answers vary.  One possible answer: <m>[0,24]</m> or <m>0 \le m \le 24</m>
            </p>
        </answer>
    </task>
     <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                What is the practical range; answer in interval or inequality notation? (How does the domain factor into finding the range?)
            </p>
        </statement>
        <answer>
            <p>
                Answers vary.  One possible answer to go with the previous domain: <m>C(0)=15</m> and <m>C(24)=134.76</m>.  So the range is <m>[15,134.76]</m> or <m>15 \le C \le 134.76</m>
            </p>
        </answer>
    </task>
</exercise>
        

